# Code Conventions

## Components

- Functional components + hooks ONLY (no class components)
- Props interface: `{ComponentName}Props`
- Named exports only (no default exports)
- Colocated tests: `ComponentName.test.tsx`

## TypeScript

- Strict mode — no `any`, no `@ts-ignore`
- Prefer `type` over `interface` for simple types
- Import types: `import type { X } from "..."`

## Files

- kebab-case for files: `element-utils.ts`
- PascalCase for components: `LayerUI.tsx`

## A/B Test: conventions.mdc

- **Prompt**: "Create a component for element properties panel"
- **Result A (rule ON)**: functional component + hooks, **`{ComponentName}Props`**, **named export**, **strict types** (`import type`, no `any`), **PascalCase** component file, **colocated** `ComponentName.test.tsx` under `packages/*` when applicable
- **Result B (rule OFF)**: class component, **default export**, `any` / `@ts-ignore`, mismatched file naming (e.g. `elementPropertiesPanel.tsx`), easy to skip tests

## How to verify

After substantive changes under `packages/`:

- `yarn test:typecheck` — TypeScript
- `yarn fix` — format and lint (auto-fix)
- `yarn test:update` — full test run (snapshots if needed)

Before committing, run the above (or the repo’s build-verify skill) so CI and local checks stay green.
